      {
        "id": 214378,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-10T16:51:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Phantom5613\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/48/1906_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Phantom5613:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Realized I didn't actually give my opinions on the episode.I enjoyed it. There were plenty of good nuggets of info and story(which hopefully makes those who didn't like the last Settings episode feel better).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, there was a lot of good stuff here.</p>\n<p>I liked finding out that apparently Madame Mittermeier and Biomancer are frenemies. Feels like there's a lot of good potential there in the RPG timeline especially.</p>\n<p>The mysterious figure that saves Baron Blade, hmmmm.</p>\n<p>Finding out about Anubis' poor wife <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/frowning.png?v=12\" title=\":frowning:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":frowning:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> and that Anubis is apparently only doing half his job.</p>\n<p>The relationship between Lovecraft and Sentinels.</p>\n<p>The implication with Void shenanigans that Tactics continues to leading to a dark and terrible place.</p>",
